[h1]Living Fellows 0.26.71[/h1]
Changes since the last Workshop upload, 0.26.67.
[url=https://thorelvin.github.io/living-fellows/]Read the Field Guide[/url]

[h2]Meet EMMA[/h2]
[list]
[*]Right-click a powered desktop computer and choose Use computer. EMMA answers plain-English questions about your camp's people, injuries, supplies, jobs, power and expeditions. She remembers notes and follow-up questions. Everything runs offline: no internet connection or hosted AI.
[*]Ask her to request medical care, queue refuelling or retry a blocked job. Actions need your Y/N confirmation, and camp records are only available from computers inside camp. Busy medics keep their current patients; confirmations recheck availability.
[*]Explore 340 original entries from 85 previous owners, plus 16 county and EMMA files. About 40% of newly discovered computers outside camp are password-locked. Electrical skill helps with recovery; failed attempts lock the machine for one game hour. Locks and files stay with a computer when moved.
[*]A full-screen 1993 terminal with large, resolution-scaled text, animated startup, boot audio, CRT glass and a beige monitor frame. Green, golden sand, aquamarine and rare purple screens pair with 195 company, camp and sector identities. Click menu choices or press their numbers; Tab switches focus.
[*]Companions can read local files at accessible, unlocked camp computers during quiet breaks. They share machines, give way when you open one, and stop for danger, orders or power loss.
[/list]

[h2]Bandits2 and Project A-Life[/h2]
[list]
[*]Optional compatibility with official Bandits2 core and Project A-Life 1.4.6 for 42.21.0 single-player. LF characters recognize their NPCs as people, respond to hostile humans and protect friendly bystanders. Each mod keeps its own characters and equipment.
[*]Supported integrations activate automatically and can be disabled in Options. Use one external NPC mod at a time. Multiplayer and other Bandits overhauls are outside this support scope.
[/list]

[h2]Combat[/h2]
[list]
[*]Fixed companion shots using another character's aim or muzzle context. Standing targets use chest-height aim, and aim stays current between shots. Native accuracy, armour and damage still apply.
[*]Human combat reloads empty guns, clears jams and switches to a usable carried weapon when ammunition runs out. Melee fighters close the distance before swinging.
[*]Companions can escape hostile humans or defend themselves when cornered. Hold Fire, protected firing lanes and household territory limits remain in effect. Distant Bandits no longer repeatedly interrupt wound treatment.
[/list]

[h2]Camp and movement fixes[/h2]
[list]
[*]Marked storage and work areas no longer flash when the companion menu refreshes, especially with the Base tab open.
[*]Infection-crisis details and choices refresh when they change, while ordinary health and hunger updates keep the Base controls stable.
[*]Right-click a marked container and choose Base life → Unmark storage. Its contents stay in place; active jobs explain when removal must wait.
[*]Companions finish getting out of bed before moving away. Those already stranded inside a mattress can recover to a clear adjacent tile without crossing walls or changing rooms.
[*]Expeditions give an active path search time to finish instead of repeatedly restarting it after eight seconds without movement.
[/list]

[b]Known limits:[/b] Difficult driving routes can still leave the car behind or interrupt a safe return. Full live acceptance for the NPC integrations remains incomplete.

[b]Updating:[/b] Project Zomboid 42.21.0, single-player. Restart the game fully after updating. Standalone users should rerun the latest Install.bat. Workshop requires ZombieBuddy 2.3.3 or newer with its one-time loader setup.
